                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "vitrioliques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "99d4d52e-ddae-34f7-9274-39165e8d875c",
                        "entry_id": "c4e9771c-b00e-36a8-970f-366564307d50",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à l’huile de vitriol ou à sa nature caustique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14da4a44-d8c3-4b5f-a708-b1bd318ac88b",
                                "sense_id": "99d4d52e-ddae-34f7-9274-39165e8d875c",
                                "text": "On sçait que le colcothar est une substance vitriolique ; ou , pour mieux dire , c'est un véritable vitriol que l'on rougit en le poussant par le feu jusqu'à un certain degré."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cddac6b3-6a60-43e7-ace5-def96f6e81c2",
                                "sense_id": "99d4d52e-ddae-34f7-9274-39165e8d875c",
                                "text": "J'ai reconnu la présence de l'alumine dans l’émeraudine de Limoges, en la vitriolisant à deux reprises, par la distillation avec deux parties d’acide vitriolique concentré; ce qui indique, que cette pierre contenait par quintal un vingtième d’alumine : […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d62dfc4b-1975-41bd-ae07-81d7db3b2b3a",
                                "sense_id": "99d4d52e-ddae-34f7-9274-39165e8d875c",
                                "text": "De tous les sels ammoniacaux, celui que la nature nous présente en plus grande quantité est le sel ammoniac formé de l’acide marin et de l’alcali volatil : les autres qui sont composés de ce même alcali avec l’acide vitriolique, l’acide nitreux, ou avec les acides végétaux et animaux, n'existent pas sur la terre, ou ne s'y trouvent qu'en si petite quantité, qu'on peut les négliger dans l'énumération des productions de la nature."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e8c23ba-74b2-34a9-b1ad-48b1be140249",
                        "entry_id": "c4e9771c-b00e-36a8-970f-366564307d50",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui attaque comme au vitriol."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e8e0c6b-933c-434f-b9bf-2fa7b429c203",
                                "sense_id": "0e8c23ba-74b2-34a9-b1ad-48b1be140249",
                                "text": "De plus, dans un livre « vitriolique » sur les pseudosciences et le paranormal, le sceptique Alain Cuniot se demande lui aussi de quelle source provient cette phrase « inconnue des physiciens »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a033b4d9-82b0-406c-95e6-13b8a269f44c",
                                "sense_id": "0e8c23ba-74b2-34a9-b1ad-48b1be140249",
                                "text": "Une des membres du CAD, Sibel Ataogul, militante QS de la première heure, a accordé une entrevue vitriolique à la revue Presse-toi à gauche, le 29 avril."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc3f8faa-5651-45f1-b7b4-0442371fe6ef",
                                "sense_id": "0e8c23ba-74b2-34a9-b1ad-48b1be140249",
                                "text": "Son journal, bien sûr, porte la trace de cette douleur, de ce mal-être qui souvent l’assaille.\nMais faut-il oublier pour autant […] ? Faut-il négliger la jeune femme à la dent dure qui savait tracer en quelques mots un portrait drôle et vitriolique de ses contemporains ? […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e3723772-774a-412d-a483-d4d8e38707e1",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4e9771c-b00e-36a8-970f-366564307d50",
                        "target_lang_word": "vitriolic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vitriolic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eafaf944-8300-3ce4-8616-bdaa8f01ccff",
                                        "entry_id": "0e9746c1-dd48-328b-bfbd-5db5d3d50536",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to vitriol; derived from or resembling vitriol."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9cfa90c-615f-4f08-bcfe-0d3f7d92d14a",
                                                "sense_id": "eafaf944-8300-3ce4-8616-bdaa8f01ccff",
                                                "text": "a vitriolic taste"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be403254-a818-4070-ac52-4f9c979dee09",
                                                "sense_id": "eafaf944-8300-3ce4-8616-bdaa8f01ccff",
                                                "text": "No one, who uſes his Senses, can possibly doubt, but there is ſomewhat of a vitriolic Nature found in Mineral Waters: for not only the Taſte, but the Sight confirms it, by their turning inky with Galls, &c."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "027a51b1-0dfe-4b68-b92a-938f09f18d63",
                                                "sense_id": "eafaf944-8300-3ce4-8616-bdaa8f01ccff",
                                                "text": "Nature, far from being confined to the lapis pyrites, has abundant materials, and a great variety of them, in the bowels of the earth, wherewith to impregnate the waters called chalybeate and vitriolic; and thoſe of various degrees of acidity and ſtypticity, even from the mildeſt, where the acid is ſcarcely ſenſible, to the moſt ſharp and cauſtic of the vitriolic ores above enumerated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9ad29d3-e233-4cac-b00b-fee96b9b1e1d",
                                                "sense_id": "eafaf944-8300-3ce4-8616-bdaa8f01ccff",
                                                "text": "[T]he name vitriol ought to be applied to all vitriolic ſalts with metallic baſes. Thus, for inſtance, the ſalt compoſed of vitriolic acid and gold may be called vitriol of gold; and the ſalt formed by the union of this acid with ſilver may be called vitriol of ſilver, or lunar vitriol. Perhaps all vitriolic ſalts might be conveniently comprehended under the general name vitriol."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "250ff208-f430-4bbb-aae7-605462973855",
                                                "sense_id": "eafaf944-8300-3ce4-8616-bdaa8f01ccff",
                                                "text": "And be it further enacted, That all and every Maker and Makers of Oxygenated Muriatic Acid or Oxymuriate of Lime respectively ſhall, before he, ſhe or they ſhall begin to mix with Salt any Vitriolic Acid, Manganese or Water, give to the Officer of Exciſe under whoſe Survey he, ſhe or they ſhall then be, Six Hours' previous Notice in Writing, if his, her or their Premiſes in which ſuch Salt ſhall be intended to be mixed with Vitriolic Acid, Manganeſe, or Water, ſhall be ſituate within the Limits of the Chief Office of Exciſe in London, or within the Limits of the City of Edinburgh; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca637349-152f-3fa5-ac87-c1dfbef28779",
                                        "entry_id": "0e9746c1-dd48-328b-bfbd-5db5d3d50536",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bitterly scathing, caustic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20deac05-bef7-4efd-bd19-3c18a4ec11f8",
                                                "sense_id": "ca637349-152f-3fa5-ac87-c1dfbef28779",
                                                "text": "vitriolic criticism"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f845032-3605-40d3-ab7f-f67bf3ea9871",
                                                "sense_id": "ca637349-152f-3fa5-ac87-c1dfbef28779",
                                                "text": "You vitriolic, patriotic, slam fight, bright light / Feeling pretty psyched"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5260d7bb-16a7-405a-a82b-d3523e8e79f6",
                                                "sense_id": "ca637349-152f-3fa5-ac87-c1dfbef28779",
                                                "text": "Another consideration is the known transparency of the Matthaean text. Because of the very structure and tone of the attack on the scribes and Pharisees, one cannot discount the possibility that Matthew is also engaged in serious controversies with the religious leadership of his own day. Therefore, consideration should also be given to the rhetoric of ancient Jewish polemic. This would account for the highly vitriolic nature of the condemnation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f6a3db3-0083-4734-9a78-6ebf5b123840",
                                                "sense_id": "ca637349-152f-3fa5-ac87-c1dfbef28779",
                                                "text": "Same-sex marriage is at the vortex of a vitriolic debate in mainline Christian denominations in the United States. Both those who advocate for same-sex marriage and those who repudiate it employ naturalizing discourses to legitimize their claims."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6b25f0a-b052-4563-97e9-ed677b4a6643",
                                                "sense_id": "ca637349-152f-3fa5-ac87-c1dfbef28779",
                                                "text": "Throughout his life, Josiah [Clark] Nott corresponded with many interesting and outstanding men of science. He became embroiled with the leaders of Protestant orthodoxy in a vitriolic argument over the unity of mankind. Nott believed that the races were created separately, as opposed to the biblical idea that all humankind came from Adam and Eve."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
